        "id": "ch11_3_2-3",
        "text": "whoami\nwindows10lab\\admin\nRunning As in Windows\nIf you\u2019re running as a low-privilege user and have administrator credentials (the\nusername and password), then you can use those credentials to escalate your\nprivilege. The most practical way is to copy a reverse shell first (for example,\nnetcat or one generated using MSFvenom). After that, connect to another\nlistening shell on your Kali host by using the runas.exe executable to run\nnetcat as another user.\nIn this example, we first started a netcat listener on Kali using port number\n6666. Next, using our limited shell, we will connect to this listener using the\nadmin credentials:\nFigure 11.5: Iperius \u2013 Evil.bat Config\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Running As in Windows\n\u2022 PSExec Tool\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
